 built deterministically: each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order joins"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it has no self-loop and no neighbour in the set yet. On a graph without self-loops it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also a minimal dominating set. O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalIndependentSet()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"maximalIndependentSet()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum dominating set: of the smallest dominating sets, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least by vertex index (the rule of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do not matter;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isolated vertices are in it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier"